## Summary

Closes #90098.

This PR fixes stack overflows when large attachment data URLs pass through full-payload regular expressions. It is deliberately limited to the behavior still missing from `main`:

- parse Gateway and Control UI data URLs with bounded index/slice logic;
- validate pasted-image base64 iteratively instead of capturing the full payload in a regex;
- discard stale failed composer queue entries created by the historical `Maximum call stack size exceeded` attachment failure;
- cover the Gateway, send, paste, and queue-migration paths with focused regressions.

Current `main` already owns the broader 20 MB / 20-page inbound extraction policy, so this branch keeps those upstream implementations and does not reintroduce obsolete extraction-limit/config changes.

## What Problem This Solves

Multi-megabyte PDF and image data URLs could be captured by regexes spanning the entire base64 payload. On sufficiently large browser or Gateway sends, V8 could throw `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` before normal attachment validation or offload handling ran. The Control UI could also restore and replay failed queue records created by that old behavior.

## Why This Change Was Made

The parser now bounds regex work to short headers and handles large payloads through index/slice or iterative validation. Queue cleanup is narrowly keyed to the identifiable pre-fix attachment failure and preserves current marked failures, unrelated text failures, and the public queue snapshot contract.

## User Impact

Large supported attachments can proceed to normal size validation/offload instead of failing in the regex engine. After upgrade, stale queue entries from this specific historical stack-overflow path are removed rather than repeatedly replayed.

## Current Changed Paths

- `src/gateway/chat-attachments.ts`
- `src/gateway/chat-attachments.test.ts`
- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.ts`
- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts`
- `ui/src/pages/chat/components/chat-composer.ts`
- `ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts`
- `ui/src/pages/chat/composer-persistence.ts`
- `ui/src/pages/chat/composer-persistence.test.ts`

## Evidence

Exact head: `1b49877519805c5feb71760a90c17697aa1c488e`.

Latest-main refresh:

- merged upstream `main` at `6c884691105b52ede83d332283d492c84d83cab9`;
- reconciled current Control UI large-text paste and attachment-removal work with the stack-safe image parser and tests;
- retained the bounded Gateway parser;
- inherited the upstream `schema_version` SQLite test-helper fix, so that unrelated helper is no longer in this PR diff;
- GitHub now reports the PR mergeable with eight focused changed paths and no unresolved review threads.

Exact-head hosted validation:

- CI run [#294987](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216691976): all 30 jobs passed, including `build-artifacts`, `checks-ui`, `check-test-types`, `check-prod-types`, `check-lint`, guards, boundary checks, QA smoke profiles, and Node test shards;
- [CodeQL](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216692004): passed;
- [CodeQL Critical Quality](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216692013): passed;
- [OpenGrep PR Diff](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216691981): passed;
- Workflow Sanity, iOS Periphery, macOS Periphery, and Shared OpenClawKit Periphery: passed.

Focused regression proof from the immediately preceding repair head `f797fa0846a3081671a4e714dbf622c3a2a1dc90`:

- `pnpm test -- src/gateway/chat-attachments.test.ts` -> 4 files / 124 tests passed, including the 12 MiB Gateway data-URL parse/offload regression;
- `pnpm --dir ui test -- src/pages/chat/composer-persistence.test.ts src/pages/chat/chat-state.test.ts src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts` -> 226 files / 3,561 tests passed;
- targeted `oxfmt` and `pnpm check:test-types` passed.

The earlier real-browser proof used Chrome and a live Gateway with a 9.18 MB, 8-page PDF (roughly a 12 MB base64 data URL): upload completed without `RangeError`, was offloaded, and produced extracted page content. That run predates this final latest-main refresh; no new exact-head provider/device claim is being made.

Generated with AI assistance; malformed security-sensitive parsing remains fail-closed.

